# Help: DMA-BUF heaps and udmabuf, to make dma-bufs from user space
#
# A dma-buf is a buffer one driver exports and another imports, such as
# a buffer io_uring registers for NVMe to read into. DMA_SHARED_BUFFER
# has no prompt, so it is built only when something selects it, as
# DMABUF_HEAPS does. The system heap hands user space a dma-buf from
# /dev/dma_heap/system and udmabuf makes one from a memfd; neither needs
# a device.
#
# Prerequisites are inlined per the self-containment rule:
# - TMPFS=y  selects MEMFD_CREATE, which UDMABUF depends on.
#
# builtin/mem/dma-buf.config builds the system heap into the kernel.
# See: drivers/dma-buf/Kconfig
# See: drivers/dma-buf/heaps/Kconfig
# See: https://docs.kernel.org/driver-api/dma-buf.html
CONFIG_DMABUF_HEAPS=y
CONFIG_DMABUF_HEAPS_SYSTEM=m
CONFIG_UDMABUF=y
CONFIG_TMPFS=y
